// ===========================================================================
// nightshade/tools/shot.hml — THE VISUAL VERIFICATION HARNESS   (task W2-11)
// ===========================================================================
//
// This is not a debug utility. It is the primary quality instrument: the harsh
// visual critic runs it every iteration from Wave 3 on, and every art decision
// in the project is argued from its output.
//
//   hemlockc -O1 tools/shot.hml -o /tmp/shot
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --scene list
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --scene ridge_golden --out docs/shots/ridge_golden.png
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --scene muzzle_fog --cam 3,2.1,-8 --look 220,-4 \
//                                   --tod 22.0 --weather storm --seed 1337 --out /tmp/a.png
//   SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy /tmp/shot --selftest
//
// THE FIVE CONTRACTS (ARCHITECTURE.md §7, BUILD_PLAN W2-11)
//
//  1. It renders through the REAL frame path. `frame_render()` below executes
//     stages 6..28 of ARCHITECTURE.md §4 in that exact order, on the real
//     engine modules (batch / emit / shade / mesh / billboard / quad / font /
//     atlas / target / stats). There is no second renderer in this file.
//  2. Deterministic. No wall clock and no @stdlib/random reach any geometry
//     decision; every placement comes from `--seed` through the local xorshift
//     below. The same command produces byte-identical PNG bytes.
//  3. Compiled only. Run interpreted it refuses with a clear error and exit 2.
//  4. It never dies on a headless SDL failure — in particular
//     SDL_SetRelativeMouseMode always fails under SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy; that
//     is reported and rendering continues.
//  5. A screenshot without its stats report is impossible. The PNG and
//     `<out>.stats.txt` are written as a pair: if either write fails, neither
//     file survives, and the report is printed to stdout as well.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IS A WAVE-2 STAND-IN AND WHAT IS PERMANENT
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PERMANENT (the harness): the CLI, the scene registry, determinism, the
// PNG+stats pairing, the compiled-only guard, the stage order of frame_render,
// the stats plumbing, `--selftest`.
//
// STAND-IN (the *content*), all of it between the two fences marked
// `WAVE-2 STAND-IN CONTENT`. In Wave 2 the game's art pipeline does not exist
// yet: src/art/palette.hml (W2-3), tod.hml (W2-4), texgen.hml (W2-5),
// skygen.hml (W2-6), fxgen/hudgen (W2-7) and meshgen.hml (W2-8) are being
// written in parallel with this file and could not be imported when it was
// built. The fence therefore holds a minimal local palette, ToD keyframe
// table, texture generator, font and mesh set, transcribed from ART_BIBLE, so
// that the five money shots are actually evaluable TODAY. W3-7 re-owns this
// file: it deletes the fence, imports the real modules, and calls
// `frame_render` from src/render/world_render.hml. The call shapes inside the
// fence deliberately match the signatures in ARCHITECTURE.md §5.3 so the swap
// is mechanical.
//
// Nothing outside the fence names a colour or a game noun.
// ===========================================================================

